# What clasp must NOT upload to the Apps Script project.
#
# clasp push sends everything under rootDir by default. The test suite is Node
# code — require(), module.exports, a fake SpreadsheetApp — and Apps Script would
# either fail to load it or, worse, pull its helper names into the same global
# namespace the real files share. Either way the add-on breaks, and the symptom
# is a project that stops running with no obvious cause.
#
# Paths are relative to rootDir (addon/). Negation is not supported reliably —
# list what to exclude, not what to keep.

test/**
**/*.test.js

# The bundler and its output. bundle.js is Node code for the same reason the
# tests are, and dist/Claude.gs is every other .gs concatenated -- pushing it
# would define every function twice in one shared namespace.
bundle.js
dist/**

# Local-only config: .clasp.json holds your own script ID.
.clasp.json
.clasp.json.example

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
